    family-names: Reuter
  - given-names: Tejvir
    family-names: Mann
abstract: >-
  A Carpentries Incubator lesson on working effectively and
  safely with AI coding agents as a researcher. Covers what
  agentic coding is, limiting what an agent can access,
  trust in packages, models, and providers, planning with
  agents, feature-based development and prompting,
  verification and testing (including test-driven
  development for research code), MCP tools and skills,
  cost, context, and energy, and what the research shows.
  This lesson is the "Agentic Coding: (Developing) Best
  Practices" workshop at the UW-Madison ML Marathon, first
  taught there in September 2026. Zekai Otles contributed
  the dev container setup.
